# Where the Battlefield 6 catalog comes from

The list was first read on **2026-10-10** (checked a second time that day
against EA's own pages) and brought up to Season 5, with pictures, on
**2026-10-21**. `catalog.json` is the single-kind form
(`kind: "weapons"`, Warzone's shape): Battlefield 6 is not built around
characters. Its four classes (Assault, Engineer, Support, Recon) each have a
signature weapon class under closed-weapon rules, but most playlists let any
class carry any gun, and the class shows only as a small icon in the squad
list, so the guns are the list.

**Pictures: publisher artwork only (decision D116).** Every picture in
`weapons/` is EA's own image, downloaded on 2026-10-21 from EA's image server
drop-assets.ea.com as used by the ea.com/games/battlefield news pages, converted
to PNG, cropped to the weapon and scaled to at most 480 x 300 pixels. None came
from a fan wiki, Fandom, a loadout site or an image search. They are EA's
copyright, used in the app to identify the weapon, the same risk the owner
accepted in D116. Delete a `.png` and set that weapon's `image` to `null` and
the app shows the class symbol instead. 31 of the 84 items have one; the rest
are listed under "No official picture" below.

## What is in Battlefield 6 today

- **Season 5, "Siege of Vegas"**, live since **2026-10-13** with Game
  Update 2.1.1.0 ([EA's 2.1.1.0 notes](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/battlefield-6-game-update-2-1-1-0),
  dated 2026-10-12, read 2026-10-21; [EA's Season 5 roadmap](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/battlefield-season-5-roadmap)).
  Its four guns are in the catalog, each at the end of its group:
  **Mk 24** (Assault Rifle), **RSPR** (SMG; the notes call it a Personal
  Defence Weapon), **Z84M** (LMG; "belt-fed", so `fireMode` auto like the
  other belt-fed LMGs) and **ELR-40** (bolt-action Sniper Rifle). The Dead
  Space event's DS-23 Pulse Rifle (from 2026-10-20) is a Battle Pickup and,
  like Season 1's, is left out. EA's Loadout Creation page still says
  "Recently Updated for Season 4" and does not list the Season 5 guns yet.
- Before it, **Season 4**, whose third and last phase was **Tidal Strike**
  (from 2026-09-15). The season's phases were Pacific Front (2026-07-21), Top Gun
  (2026-08-18) and Tidal Strike ([EA's Season 4 roadmap](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/season-4-roadmap-everything-you-need-to-know),
  [EA's Tidal Strike guide](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/redsec/news/battlefield-season-4-update-event-guide)).
  `season` is now "Season 5: Siege of Vegas".
- **84 items in 10 groups**: Assault Rifles 12, Carbines 9, SMGs 11, LMGs 11,
  DMRs 6, Sniper Rifles 7, Shotguns 4, Sidearms 7, Gadget weapons 11 (the
  launchers and the SS26, which replace the gun in the player's hands and the
  HUD's weapon panel), Melee 6.

### The names: EA's own weapon list

EA's [Loadout Creation and Weapon Classes](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/loadout-creation-and-weapon-classes)
page ("Recently Updated for Season 4", 2026-07-21) lists every gun by class
with its unlock. It is the first source of every gun and sidearm, and its
spelling wins. It settled every name the first pass had marked uncertain:

| Was uncertain | EA writes | Other spellings seen |
|---|---|---|
| NVO-228E | NVO-228E | NVO-228 (beta lists) |
| M277 | M277 (Career Rank 11) | M227 |
| SOR-300SC | SOR-300SC | SOR-300C (EA's own Season 1 roadmap) |
| BROD 3 | BROD 3 (also EA's Season 4 roadmap, "Carbine Rifle") | BRD 3, BREN 3 |
| Mini Scout | Mini Scout (also EA's Season 1 roadmap) | Mini Fix |
| GRT-CPS | GRT-CPS (also EA's Season 2 roadmap) | CRT-CPS |
| M357 Trait | M357 TRAIT | M327 Trait (EA's Season 1 roadmap) |
| SL9 | SL9, under SMG | - |
| Interdictor | Interdictor, Sniper Rifle, "Available During Season 4 Event" (Top Gun) | - |
| VZ.61 | vz. 61, under Secondary (EA's Season 2 roadmap: "NEW SIDEARM: VZ.61", a machine pistol) | VZ.61 |

It also changed three names: **M60 is "M/60"**, **L115 is "L115A3"** and
**18.5 KS-K is "18.5KS-K"** (ids changed with them; nothing has shipped).
Where EA's roadmaps spelt a gun differently from the newer loadout page
(SOR-300C, M327 Trait), the newer page is taken as the game's current name.

Settled on 2026-10-21 from EA's own pages:

- **RPKM** (launch LMG): EA's [Progression in Battlefield 6](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/progression-in-battlefield-6)
  lists "RPKM, Weapon, LMG" at Rank 30, and EA's [Season 3 roadmap](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/season-3-roadmap-everything-you-need-to-know)
  calls the RPK-74M "a powerful complement to the RPKM". No longer uncertain.
- **X95 BRE** (Assault gadget, was "X95 BRM"): EA writes "X95 BRE Breaching
  Projectile Launcher" in the [1.1.2.0 notes](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/battlefield-6-game-update-1-1-2-0)
  and "Gadget Skin - X95 BRE" in the [Season 3 Battle Pass page](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/battlefield-6-redsec-season-3-battle-pass-everything-you-need-to-know).
  The name changed; the id `gadget_weapons.x95_brm` did not (ids never
  change), and "X95 BRM" stays as an alias for search.
- **Royal Navy Dive Knife**: EA's [Season 4 page](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/seasons/bf6-season-4)
  calls it "the new Royal Navy Dive Knife" and the roadmap files its picture
  as `..._NewMelee_DiveKnife.jpg`, so it is a melee weapon, not a skin. The
  2.1.1.0 notes add to Portal "the Season 4 Battle Pass weapons: EF88 ...
  Interdictor ... and Hadal NV-08 Knife"; that list also names the Interdictor,
  an event reward, and no other Season 4 knife exists, so **"Hadal NV-08
  Knife" is taken as its in-game name** and added as an alias (still marked
  uncertain: not seen on screen).

Still uncertain:
- **Melee.** EA's loadout page lists COMBAT KNIFE, HUNTING KNIFE, NOMAD CX-12
  ICE-CLIMBING AXE and SLEDGEHAMMER. The axe is "Ice Climbing Axe" in the
  Season 1 roadmap and "NOMAD CX-12 Ice Axe" in Season 2's. The Season 2
  machete was announced as the "KAPOK 14” Machete", but the
  [Hunter / Prey bonus path](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/season-2-hunter-prey-bonus-path-free-challenges-guide)
  that delivered it names its reward "Ripper 14”" (a "Serrated Blade"); they
  are taken as one weapon. The Royal Navy Dive Knife is the Deep Six event's
  final reward (EA: 2026-09-15 to 09-29); EA does not say whether it is a
  weapon or a skin. Guides call the default knife the KBR Mark II.

Battle Pickups (Season 1's Rorsch Mk-2 SMRW railgun and MP-RMG minigun) are
found on the map, not equipped, and are left out.

- **Gadgets** are from [MP1st's launch gadget list](https://mp1st.com/news/battlefield-6-gadgets-list-for-all-classes-available-at-launch)
  (EA publishes none); the 9K38 IGLA from EA's Season 2 roadmap ("9K38 IGLA
  ACTIVE LOCKING AIR-DEFENSE LAUNCHER", Engineer).
- **Fire modes** are set only where the class settles it (bolt snipers, semi
  DMRs and sidearms, pump shotguns, belt-fed LMGs) and for the M16A4 (burst,
  full-auto only with an attachment). Battlefield's guns switch modes in game
  and no source lists them gun by gun.
- The Battlefield wiki (HTTP 402) and EA's forums (HTTP 403) would not load.

| Class | Signature (closed weapons) |
|---|---|
| Assault | Assault Rifles |
| Engineer | SMGs |
| Support | LMGs |
| Recon | Sniper Rifles |

([EA's class guide](https://help.ea.com/en/articles/battlefield/battlefield-6/class-guide/))

